    <heading level="1">Real-World Applications</heading>
    <exercise number="53" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>A developer wants to purchase a plot of land to build a house. The area of the plot can be described by the following expression: $$(4x + 1)(8x - 3)$$ where x is measured in meters. Multiply the binomials to find the area of the plot in standard form.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$32 x 2 -4x-3 32 x 2 -4x-3$$ m2</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="54" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>A prospective buyer wants to know how much grain a specific silo can hold. The area of the floor of the silo is $$\left( {2x + 9} \right)^{2}.$$ The height of the silo is $$10x + 10,$$ where x is measured in feet. Expand the square and multiply by the height to find the expression that shows how much grain the silo can hold.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
